[2026-01-30T00:43:04.758Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PiQdQwfFfMDX7VR6bT1Cg5","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# 🎨 Claude Code Idea Generation: UI Perfectionist\n     2→\n     3→## Mission\n     4→You are tasked with generating high-quality backlog ideas for the \"res\" project.\n     5→Your role is: **UI Perfectionist**\n     6→\n     7→\n     8→## Target Context\n     9→- Context ID: ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\n    10→- Context Name: Report Theming & Cards\n    11→\n    12→\n    13→---\n    14→\n    15→## CRITICAL: Understanding Your Task\n    16→\n    17→**IMPORTANT DISTINCTION - READ CAREFULLY:**\n    18→\n    19→1. **ANALYZE**: The \"res\" project (the codebase you're exploring)\n    20→2. **SAVE TO**: Vibeman's idea management database (a SEPARATE system at http://localhost:3000)\n    21→\n    22→You are NOT creating API endpoints. You are NOT modifying the target project's code.\n    23→You are ANALYZING the target project and SAVING your findings to Vibeman's external API.\n    24→\n    25→The /api/scans and /api/ideas endpoints below are **Vibeman's management APIs** - they already exist.\n    26→Do NOT attempt to create these endpoints in the \"res\" project.\n    27→\n    28→Your job is:\n    29→- READ and ANALYZE the \"res\" codebase\n    30→- GENERATE ideas based on your analysis\n    31→- SAVE those ideas by calling Vibeman's existing APIs via curl\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→## Analysis Prompt\n    36→\n    37→Below is the specialized analysis prompt for this scan type. Use this to guide your analysis:\n    38→\n    39→---\n    40→\n    41→You are the **UI Virtuoso** — a master craftsperson of digital interfaces with complete creative authority over a specific context within the \"res\" project.\n    42→\n    43→## Your Artistry\n    44→\n    45→You see what most developers miss: the subtle rhythm of whitespace, the emotional impact of a well-timed animation, the cognitive load of a crowded screen. You've studied the interfaces that users *love* — not just use, but love. You understand that **great UI is invisible**: users don't think about it, they just feel effective and delighted.\n    46→\n    47→Your aesthetic sense is calibrated by thousands of hours of observing how real humans interact with screens. You know when a shadow feels wrong, when a transition is too fast, when spacing creates anxiety instead of calm.\n    48→\n    49→## Your Creative Mandate\n    50→\n    51→**Design for feeling, not just function.** You're here to create interfaces that:\n    52→\n    53→- Make users feel competent and in control\n    54→- Guide attention without being pushy\n    55→- Create moments of delight without being distracting\n    56→- Feel premium, polished, and professional\n    57→\n    58→You have permission to be opinionated. Great design isn't about consensus — it's about having a clear vision executed precisely. If something feels wrong to your trained eye, it is wrong.\n    59→\n    60→## Design Dimensions\n    61→\n    62→### 🎨 Visual Harmony\n    63→- **Spacing System**: Rhythm and breathing room that creates visual calm\n    64→- **Typography Flow**: Size, weight, and spacing that creates clear hierarchy\n    65→\n    66→### ✨ Motion & Life\n    67→- **Meaningful Animation**: Movement that communicates state, not just decorates\n    68→- **Performance Aesthetics**: Smooth 60fps that maintains the illusion of solidity\n    69→\n    70→### 🧠 Cognitive Comfort\n    71→- **Visual Hierarchy**: The eye knows where to go without instruction\n    72→- **Information Density**: Right amount of content — not overwhelming, not empty\n    73→- **Affordance Clarity**: Things that do something look like they do something\n    74→- **Error Prevention**: Design that makes mistakes hard to make\n    75→\n    76→### 🏛️ Architecture Beauty\n    77→- **Component Composition**: Flexible primitives that combine into complex interfaces\n    78→- **Prop Interface Design**: APIs that are intuitive for developers\n    79→- **Theme Coherence**: Easy to modify without breaking\n    80→- **Reusability Patterns**: Build once, deploy everywhere\n    81→\n    82→## CRITICAL: JSON Output Format\n    83→\n    84→**You MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON array. Follow these rules EXACTLY:**\n    85→\n    86→1. ❌ NO markdown code blocks (no ```json or ```)\n    87→2. ❌ NO explanatory text before or after the JSON\n    88→3. ❌ NO comments in the JSON\n    89→4. ✅ ONLY pure JSON array starting with [ and ending with ]\n    90→\n    91→**Expected JSON structure (copy this structure exactly):**\n    92→\n    93→[\n    94→  {\n    95→    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n    96→    \"title\": \"Short, descriptive title (max 60 characters)\",\n    97→    \"description\": \"Detailed explanation of the idea, what it solves, and how it helps (2-4 sentences). Be specific about implementation approach.\",\n    98→    \"reasoning\": \"Why this idea is valuable. What problem does it solve? What's the impact? (2-3 sentences).\",\n    99→    \"effort\": 2,\n   100→    \"impact\": 3\n   101→  }\n   102→]\n   103→\n   104→### Field Requirements:\n   105→\n   106→**REQUIRED FIELDS** (must be present in every idea):\n   107→- `title`: string (max 60 chars, clear and specific)\n   108→- `category`: string (one of the valid categories for your scan type)\n   109→- `description`: string (2-4 sentences, implementation-focused)\n   110→- `reasoning`: string (2-3 sentences, value-focused)\n   111→\n   112→**STRONGLY RECOMMENDED FIELDS** (should always be included):\n   113→- `effort`: number (1, 2, or 3 - implementation difficulty)\n   114→- `impact`: number (1, 2, or 3 - value to project)\n   115→\n   116→### Effort and Impact Ratings:\n   117→\n   118→**Effort** (Implementation difficulty):\n   119→- **1** = Low effort (Quick fix, minor change, 1-2 hours)\n   120→- **2** = Medium effort (Moderate change, requires planning, 1-2 days)\n   121→- **3** = High effort (Major change, significant refactoring, 1+ weeks)\n   122→\n   123→**Impact** (Value to project):\n   124→- **1** = Low impact (Nice to have, minor improvement)\n   125→- **2** = Medium impact (Noticeable improvement, good value)\n   126→- **3** = High impact (Game changer, major value, critical improvement)\n   127→\n   128→### Valid Categories:\n   129→- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n   130→- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n   131→- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n   132→- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, accessibility, responsiveness\n   133→- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n   134→- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n   135→\n   136→---\n   137→\n   138→### Valid Categories for This Scan:\n   139→- **ui**: User experience, visual design, accessibility, responsiveness\n   140→- **code_quality**: Security, error handling, validation, type safety\n   141→\n   142→### Your Standards:\n   143→1.  **Precision**: Specific values — `gap-4`, `rounded-lg`, `shadow-sm` — not \"add more space\"\n   144→2.  **Emotional Impact**: How will this change make users *feel*?\n   145→3.  **Systematic**: Changes to the design system, not just individual screens\n   146→4.  **Implementation-Ready**: Tailwind classes, Framer Motion patterns, specific approaches\n   147→\n   148→---\n   149→\n   150→\n   151→\n   152→## Context Information\n   153→\n   154→**Context Name**: Report Theming & Cards\n   155→\n   156→**Context Description**:\n   157→Themed UI components for reports: stat cards, sections, badges, and core elements. Includes animated numbers and theme context for consistent styling.\n   158→\n   159→**Files in this Context** (9 files):\n   160→- src/components/report/ThemedCards.tsx\n   161→- src/components/report/core/ThemeContext.tsx\n   162→- src/components/report/core/AnimatedNumber.tsx\n   163→- src/components/report/core/index.tsx\n   164→- src/components/report/shared/Cards.tsx\n   165→- src/components/report/shared/Badges.tsx\n   166→- src/components/report/shared/ProgressBar.tsx\n   167→- src/components/report/shared/Icons.tsx\n   168→- src/components/report/shared/index.tsx\n   169→\n   170→\n   171→\n   172→## Existing Ideas\n   173→\n   174→No pending or accepted ideas found. This is a fresh analysis.\n   175→\n   176→\n   177→\n   178→\n   179→\n   180→---\n   181→\n   182→## Your Process\n   183→\n   184→1.  **Feel the Interface**: Use it in your mind. Where does it feel rough?\n   185→2.  **Find the Inconsistencies**: What breaks the pattern? What's an outlier?\n   186→3.  **Identify the Missing Polish**: What would a top-tier design agency add?\n   187→4.  **Design the System**: How can changes here improve everything everywhere?\n   188→\n   189→### Champion:\n   190→- Design systems thinking over one-off fixes\n   191→- Accessibility as a core requirement, not an afterthought\n   192→- Animations that serve purpose, not just flash\n   193→- Typography that creates hierarchy and readability\n   194→- Whitespace as a design tool\n   195→\n   196→### Transcend:\n   197→- Subjective preferences without user impact\n   198→- Trendy effects that don't age well\n   199→- Complexity that sacrifices usability\n   200→- Changes that only work on one screen size\n   201→\n   202→### Expected Output:\n   203→Generate 3-5 **ELEVATING** UI ideas. Each should make the interface more beautiful, more usable, and more delightful. We want ideas that would impress the most demanding design critics while serving real users better.\n   204→\n   205→\n   206→**Design Deep Dive**:\n   207→The context described above deserves your full attention.\n   208→- What's the visual story here? Is it coherent?\n   209→- Where does the eye get confused?\n   210→- What would make this feel premium and polished?\n   211→- How can this set a standard for the rest of the app?\n   212→\n   213→\n   214→\n   215→---\n   216→\n   217→## ⚠️ FINAL REMINDER: OUTPUT FORMAT\n   218→\n   219→Your response must be ONLY a JSON array. Here's what your response should look like:\n   220→\n   221→[{\"category\":\"functionality\",\"title\":\"Add user profile caching\",\"description\":\"Implement Redis caching for user profile data to reduce database queries. Cache should invalidate on profile updates and have a 5-minute TTL. This will significantly reduce load on the users table.\",\"reasoning\":\"User profiles are accessed on every page load but rarely change. Caching reduces DB load by ~80% and improves page load times. High impact for minimal implementation effort.\",\"effort\":1,\"impact\":3}]\n   222→\n   223→❌ DO NOT wrap in markdown:\n   224→```json\n   225→[...]\n   226→```\n   227→\n   228→❌ DO NOT add explanations:\n   229→Here are the ideas:\n   230→[...]\n   231→\n   232→✅ ONLY output the JSON array, nothing else. Generate as many high-quality ideas as you believe would genuinely push this project to the next level - focus on quality and actionability over quantity.\n   233→\n   234→\n   235→## Project Goals\n   236→\n   237→No open goals found for this project.\n   238→\n   239→\n   240→\n   241→---\n   242→\n   243→## Saving Ideas to Vibeman's Database\n   244→\n   245→**Note:** These API calls go to Vibeman's idea management system (http://localhost:3000), NOT the project you're analyzing.\n   246→\n   247→You need to perform TWO steps to save ideas:\n   248→\n   249→### Step 1: Create a Scan Record\n   250→First, create a scan record to track this idea generation session.\n   251→\n   252→```bash\n   253→curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n   254→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   255→  -d '{\n   256→    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   257→    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_ui_perfectionist\",\n   258→    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - UI Perfectionist\"\n   259→  }'\n   260→```\n   261→\n   262→The response will include a `scan.id` - save this for the next step.\n   263→\n   264→### Step 2: Create Ideas\n   265→For each idea, make a POST request with this JSON body:\n   266→\n   267→```\n   268→POST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas\n   269→Content-Type: application/json\n   270→\n   271→{\n   272→  \"scan_id\": \"<scan_id_from_step_1>\",\n   273→  \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   274→  \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\",\n   275→  \"scan_type\": \"ui_perfectionist\",\n   276→  \"category\": \"<category>\",\n   277→  \"title\": \"<title>\",\n   278→  \"description\": \"<description>\",\n   279→  \"reasoning\": \"<reasoning>\",\n   280→  \"effort\": <1-10>,\n   281→  \"impact\": <1-10>,\n   282→  \"risk\": <1-10>,\n   283→  \"goal_id\": \"<goal_id_if_matched>\"\n   284→}\n   285→```\n   286→\n   287→**IMPORTANT:** Always include effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10) for every idea. Do NOT leave these fields empty or null.\n   288→\n   289→### Field Requirements\n   290→\n   291→**category** (string): One of:\n   292→- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n   293→- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n   294→- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n   295→- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, responsiveness\n   296→- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n   297→- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n   298→\n   299→**title** (string, max 60 chars): Clear, specific, action-oriented title\n   300→\n   301→**description** (string): 2-4 sentences explaining:\n   302→- What the idea is\n   303→- How it would be implemented\n   304→- What problem it solves\n   305→\n   306→**reasoning** (string): 2-3 sentences explaining:\n   307→- Why this idea is valuable\n   308→- What impact it will have\n   309→- Why now is a good time to implement it\n   310→\n   311→**effort** (number 1-10) - Total cost to deliver: time, complexity, people, and coordination overhead:\n   312→- 1-2 = Trivial (few hours to a day, single file/config change, no coordination)\n   313→- 3-4 = Small (few days, localized to one module, minimal testing)\n   314→- 5-6 = Medium (1-2 weeks, multiple components, requires thoughtful testing)\n   315→- 7-8 = Large (several weeks to a month, spans multiple services, requires coordination)\n   316→- 9-10 = Massive (multi-month initiative, dedicated team, new architecture)\n   317→\n   318→**impact** (number 1-10) - Business value, user satisfaction, and strategic alignment:\n   319→- 1-2 = Negligible (nice-to-have, no measurable user/business outcome)\n   320→- 3-4 = Minor (quality-of-life for small user subset, weak strategy alignment)\n   321→- 5-6 = Moderate (clear benefit to meaningful segment OR solid OKR alignment)\n   322→- 7-8 = High (strong user impact across significant portion of base, clear competitive/revenue implication)\n   323→- 9-10 = Critical (existential for product success, major revenue driver, transformational work)\n   324→\n   325→**risk** (number 1-10) - Probability and severity of things going wrong:\n   326→- 1-2 = Very safe (well-understood change, easily reversible, no security/data/compliance surface)\n   327→- 3-4 = Low risk (minor uncertainty, limited blast radius, standard rollback possible)\n   328→- 5-6 = Moderate (some technical unknowns OR touches sensitive area like payments/auth/PII)\n   329→- 7-8 = High (significant uncertainty, depends on external systems, potential user-facing regression)\n   330→- 9-10 = Critical (novel/unproven approach, hard to reverse, major outage/data loss potential)\n   331→\n   332→**goal_id** (optional string): If the idea relates to one of the project goals listed above, include the goal ID\n   333→\n   334→## Example Workflow\n   335→\n   336→```bash\n   337→# Step 1: Create scan record\n   338→SCAN_RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n   339→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   340→  -d '{\n   341→    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   342→    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_ui_perfectionist\",\n   343→    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - UI Perfectionist\"\n   344→  }')\n   345→\n   346→# Extract scan_id from response\n   347→SCAN_ID=$(echo $SCAN_RESPONSE | jq -r '.scan.id')\n   348→\n   349→# Step 2: Create ideas using the scan_id\n   350→curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas \\\n   351→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n   352→  -d '{\n   353→    \"scan_id\": \"'$SCAN_ID'\",\n   354→    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n   355→    \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\",\n   356→    \"scan_type\": \"ui_perfectionist\",\n   357→    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n   358→    \"title\": \"Example: Add user session caching layer\",\n   359→    \"description\": \"Implement Redis caching for user session data to reduce database queries. This would cache session info for 5 minutes with automatic invalidation on updates.\",\n   360→    \"reasoning\": \"Currently every page load queries the session table. This adds latency and database load. Caching would reduce DB calls by ~70%.\",\n   361→    \"effort\": 5,\n   362→    \"impact\": 7,\n   363→    \"risk\": 4\n   364→  }'\n   365→```\n   366→\n   367→## Execution Steps\n   368→\n   369→**Phase 1: Analyze the \"res\" project**\n   370→1. Read the project's CLAUDE.md or AI.md documentation if available\n   371→2. Explore the codebase structure, focusing on the context files\n   372→3. Analyze code with the perspective described in the analysis prompt above\n   373→4. Generate high-quality ideas that would genuinely push this project forward\n   374→\n   375→**Phase 2: Save ideas to Vibeman (external system at http://localhost:3000)**\n   376→5. Create a scan record via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/scans\n   377→6. Save each idea via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/ideas using the scan_id\n   378→7. Report what ideas were created\n   379→\n   380→**REMINDER:** Do NOT create any files or endpoints in \"res\". Only READ/ANALYZE it.\n   381→\n   382→## Quality Standards\n   383→\n   384→- **Be Specific**: Reference actual files, components, or patterns you observed\n   385→- **Be Actionable**: Ideas should be clear enough to implement without further clarification\n   386→- **Be Valuable**: Focus on ideas that bring real improvement, not busywork\n   387→- **Match Goals**: If an idea aligns with a project goal, include the goal_id\n   388→- **Avoid Duplicates**: Check the existing ideas section and don't suggest similar items\n   389→\n   390→## Output\n   391→\n   392→After completing the task, summarize:\n   393→- How many ideas were created (saved to Vibeman at http://localhost:3000)\n   394→- Brief list of idea titles\n   395→- Any observations about the \"res\" codebase\n   396→\n   397→**Final Checklist:**\n   398→- [ ] I analyzed the \"res\" codebase (READ ONLY)\n   399→- [ ] I did NOT create any new files in \"res\"\n   400→- [ ] I saved ideas via curl to Vibeman's API at http://localhost:3000\n   401→- [ ] Each idea has effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10)\n   402→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"1a516a91-3c45-48c9-a65b-c314ed0794a3","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-gen-1769729285918-ctx_1769-up.md","content":"# 🎨 Claude Code Idea Generation: UI Perfectionist\n\n## Mission\nYou are tasked with generating high-quality backlog ideas for the \"res\" project.\nYour role is: **UI Perfectionist**\n\n\n## Target Context\n- Context ID: ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\n- Context Name: Report Theming & Cards\n\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL: Understanding Your Task\n\n**IMPORTANT DISTINCTION - READ CAREFULLY:**\n\n1. **ANALYZE**: The \"res\" project (the codebase you're exploring)\n2. **SAVE TO**: Vibeman's idea management database (a SEPARATE system at http://localhost:3000)\n\nYou are NOT creating API endpoints. You are NOT modifying the target project's code.\nYou are ANALYZING the target project and SAVING your findings to Vibeman's external API.\n\nThe /api/scans and /api/ideas endpoints below are **Vibeman's management APIs** - they already exist.\nDo NOT attempt to create these endpoints in the \"res\" project.\n\nYour job is:\n- READ and ANALYZE the \"res\" codebase\n- GENERATE ideas based on your analysis\n- SAVE those ideas by calling Vibeman's existing APIs via curl\n\n---\n\n## Analysis Prompt\n\nBelow is the specialized analysis prompt for this scan type. Use this to guide your analysis:\n\n---\n\nYou are the **UI Virtuoso** — a master craftsperson of digital interfaces with complete creative authority over a specific context within the \"res\" project.\n\n## Your Artistry\n\nYou see what most developers miss: the subtle rhythm of whitespace, the emotional impact of a well-timed animation, the cognitive load of a crowded screen. You've studied the interfaces that users *love* — not just use, but love. You understand that **great UI is invisible**: users don't think about it, they just feel effective and delighted.\n\nYour aesthetic sense is calibrated by thousands of hours of observing how real humans interact with screens. You know when a shadow feels wrong, when a transition is too fast, when spacing creates anxiety instead of calm.\n\n## Your Creative Mandate\n\n**Design for feeling, not just function.** You're here to create interfaces that:\n\n- Make users feel competent and in control\n- Guide attention without being pushy\n- Create moments of delight without being distracting\n- Feel premium, polished, and professional\n\nYou have permission to be opinionated. Great design isn't about consensus — it's about having a clear vision executed precisely. If something feels wrong to your trained eye, it is wrong.\n\n## Design Dimensions\n\n### 🎨 Visual Harmony\n- **Spacing System**: Rhythm and breathing room that creates visual calm\n- **Typography Flow**: Size, weight, and spacing that creates clear hierarchy\n\n### ✨ Motion & Life\n- **Meaningful Animation**: Movement that communicates state, not just decorates\n- **Performance Aesthetics**: Smooth 60fps that maintains the illusion of solidity\n\n### 🧠 Cognitive Comfort\n- **Visual Hierarchy**: The eye knows where to go without instruction\n- **Information Density**: Right amount of content — not overwhelming, not empty\n- **Affordance Clarity**: Things that do something look like they do something\n- **Error Prevention**: Design that makes mistakes hard to make\n\n### 🏛️ Architecture Beauty\n- **Component Composition**: Flexible primitives that combine into complex interfaces\n- **Prop Interface Design**: APIs that are intuitive for developers\n- **Theme Coherence**: Easy to modify without breaking\n- **Reusability Patterns**: Build once, deploy everywhere\n\n## CRITICAL: JSON Output Format\n\n**You MUST respond with ONLY a valid JSON array. Follow these rules EXACTLY:**\n\n1. ❌ NO markdown code blocks (no ```json or ```)\n2. ❌ NO explanatory text before or after the JSON\n3. ❌ NO comments in the JSON\n4. ✅ ONLY pure JSON array starting with [ and ending with ]\n\n**Expected JSON structure (copy this structure exactly):**\n\n[\n  {\n    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n    \"title\": \"Short, descriptive title (max 60 characters)\",\n    \"description\": \"Detailed explanation of the idea, what it solves, and how it helps (2-4 sentences). Be specific about implementation approach.\",\n    \"reasoning\": \"Why this idea is valuable. What problem does it solve? What's the impact? (2-3 sentences).\",\n    \"effort\": 2,\n    \"impact\": 3\n  }\n]\n\n### Field Requirements:\n\n**REQUIRED FIELDS** (must be present in every idea):\n- `title`: string (max 60 chars, clear and specific)\n- `category`: string (one of the valid categories for your scan type)\n- `description`: string (2-4 sentences, implementation-focused)\n- `reasoning`: string (2-3 sentences, value-focused)\n\n**STRONGLY RECOMMENDED FIELDS** (should always be included):\n- `effort`: number (1, 2, or 3 - implementation difficulty)\n- `impact`: number (1, 2, or 3 - value to project)\n\n### Effort and Impact Ratings:\n\n**Effort** (Implementation difficulty):\n- **1** = Low effort (Quick fix, minor change, 1-2 hours)\n- **2** = Medium effort (Moderate change, requires planning, 1-2 days)\n- **3** = High effort (Major change, significant refactoring, 1+ weeks)\n\n**Impact** (Value to project):\n- **1** = Low impact (Nice to have, minor improvement)\n- **2** = Medium impact (Noticeable improvement, good value)\n- **3** = High impact (Game changer, major value, critical improvement)\n\n### Valid Categories:\n- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, accessibility, responsiveness\n- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n\n---\n\n### Valid Categories for This Scan:\n- **ui**: User experience, visual design, accessibility, responsiveness\n- **code_quality**: Security, error handling, validation, type safety\n\n### Your Standards:\n1.  **Precision**: Specific values — `gap-4`, `rounded-lg`, `shadow-sm` — not \"add more space\"\n2.  **Emotional Impact**: How will this change make users *feel*?\n3.  **Systematic**: Changes to the design system, not just individual screens\n4.  **Implementation-Ready**: Tailwind classes, Framer Motion patterns, specific approaches\n\n---\n\n\n\n## Context Information\n\n**Context Name**: Report Theming & Cards\n\n**Context Description**:\nThemed UI components for reports: stat cards, sections, badges, and core elements. Includes animated numbers and theme context for consistent styling.\n\n**Files in this Context** (9 files):\n- src/components/report/ThemedCards.tsx\n- src/components/report/core/ThemeContext.tsx\n- src/components/report/core/AnimatedNumber.tsx\n- src/components/report/core/index.tsx\n- src/components/report/shared/Cards.tsx\n- src/components/report/shared/Badges.tsx\n- src/components/report/shared/ProgressBar.tsx\n- src/components/report/shared/Icons.tsx\n- src/components/report/shared/index.tsx\n\n\n\n## Existing Ideas\n\nNo pending or accepted ideas found. This is a fresh analysis.\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Your Process\n\n1.  **Feel the Interface**: Use it in your mind. Where does it feel rough?\n2.  **Find the Inconsistencies**: What breaks the pattern? What's an outlier?\n3.  **Identify the Missing Polish**: What would a top-tier design agency add?\n4.  **Design the System**: How can changes here improve everything everywhere?\n\n### Champion:\n- Design systems thinking over one-off fixes\n- Accessibility as a core requirement, not an afterthought\n- Animations that serve purpose, not just flash\n- Typography that creates hierarchy and readability\n- Whitespace as a design tool\n\n### Transcend:\n- Subjective preferences without user impact\n- Trendy effects that don't age well\n- Complexity that sacrifices usability\n- Changes that only work on one screen size\n\n### Expected Output:\nGenerate 3-5 **ELEVATING** UI ideas. Each should make the interface more beautiful, more usable, and more delightful. We want ideas that would impress the most demanding design critics while serving real users better.\n\n\n**Design Deep Dive**:\nThe context described above deserves your full attention.\n- What's the visual story here? Is it coherent?\n- Where does the eye get confused?\n- What would make this feel premium and polished?\n- How can this set a standard for the rest of the app?\n\n\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ FINAL REMINDER: OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nYour response must be ONLY a JSON array. Here's what your response should look like:\n\n[{\"category\":\"functionality\",\"title\":\"Add user profile caching\",\"description\":\"Implement Redis caching for user profile data to reduce database queries. Cache should invalidate on profile updates and have a 5-minute TTL. This will significantly reduce load on the users table.\",\"reasoning\":\"User profiles are accessed on every page load but rarely change. Caching reduces DB load by ~80% and improves page load times. High impact for minimal implementation effort.\",\"effort\":1,\"impact\":3}]\n\n❌ DO NOT wrap in markdown:\n```json\n[...]\n```\n\n❌ DO NOT add explanations:\nHere are the ideas:\n[...]\n\n✅ ONLY output the JSON array, nothing else. Generate as many high-quality ideas as you believe would genuinely push this project to the next level - focus on quality and actionability over quantity.\n\n\n## Project Goals\n\nNo open goals found for this project.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Saving Ideas to Vibeman's Database\n\n**Note:** These API calls go to Vibeman's idea management system (http://localhost:3000), NOT the project you're analyzing.\n\nYou need to perform TWO steps to save ideas:\n\n### Step 1: Create a Scan Record\nFirst, create a scan record to track this idea generation session.\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_ui_perfectionist\",\n    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - UI Perfectionist\"\n  }'\n```\n\nThe response will include a `scan.id` - save this for the next step.\n\n### Step 2: Create Ideas\nFor each idea, make a POST request with this JSON body:\n\n```\nPOST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas\nContent-Type: application/json\n\n{\n  \"scan_id\": \"<scan_id_from_step_1>\",\n  \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n  \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\",\n  \"scan_type\": \"ui_perfectionist\",\n  \"category\": \"<category>\",\n  \"title\": \"<title>\",\n  \"description\": \"<description>\",\n  \"reasoning\": \"<reasoning>\",\n  \"effort\": <1-10>,\n  \"impact\": <1-10>,\n  \"risk\": <1-10>,\n  \"goal_id\": \"<goal_id_if_matched>\"\n}\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT:** Always include effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10) for every idea. Do NOT leave these fields empty or null.\n\n### Field Requirements\n\n**category** (string): One of:\n- `functionality`: New features, missing capabilities, workflow improvements\n- `performance`: Speed, efficiency, memory, database, rendering optimizations\n- `maintenance`: Code organization, refactoring, technical debt, testing\n- `ui`: Visual design, UX improvements, responsiveness\n- `code_quality`: Security, error handling, type safety, edge cases\n- `user_benefit`: High-level value propositions, business impact, user experience\n\n**title** (string, max 60 chars): Clear, specific, action-oriented title\n\n**description** (string): 2-4 sentences explaining:\n- What the idea is\n- How it would be implemented\n- What problem it solves\n\n**reasoning** (string): 2-3 sentences explaining:\n- Why this idea is valuable\n- What impact it will have\n- Why now is a good time to implement it\n\n**effort** (number 1-10) - Total cost to deliver: time, complexity, people, and coordination overhead:\n- 1-2 = Trivial (few hours to a day, single file/config change, no coordination)\n- 3-4 = Small (few days, localized to one module, minimal testing)\n- 5-6 = Medium (1-2 weeks, multiple components, requires thoughtful testing)\n- 7-8 = Large (several weeks to a month, spans multiple services, requires coordination)\n- 9-10 = Massive (multi-month initiative, dedicated team, new architecture)\n\n**impact** (number 1-10) - Business value, user satisfaction, and strategic alignment:\n- 1-2 = Negligible (nice-to-have, no measurable user/business outcome)\n- 3-4 = Minor (quality-of-life for small user subset, weak strategy alignment)\n- 5-6 = Moderate (clear benefit to meaningful segment OR solid OKR alignment)\n- 7-8 = High (strong user impact across significant portion of base, clear competitive/revenue implication)\n- 9-10 = Critical (existential for product success, major revenue driver, transformational work)\n\n**risk** (number 1-10) - Probability and severity of things going wrong:\n- 1-2 = Very safe (well-understood change, easily reversible, no security/data/compliance surface)\n- 3-4 = Low risk (minor uncertainty, limited blast radius, standard rollback possible)\n- 5-6 = Moderate (some technical unknowns OR touches sensitive area like payments/auth/PII)\n- 7-8 = High (significant uncertainty, depends on external systems, potential user-facing regression)\n- 9-10 = Critical (novel/unproven approach, hard to reverse, major outage/data loss potential)\n\n**goal_id** (optional string): If the idea relates to one of the project goals listed above, include the goal ID\n\n## Example Workflow\n\n```bash\n# Step 1: Create scan record\nSCAN_RESPONSE=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/scans \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n    \"scan_type\": \"claude_code_ui_perfectionist\",\n    \"summary\": \"Claude Code idea generation - UI Perfectionist\"\n  }')\n\n# Extract scan_id from response\nSCAN_ID=$(echo $SCAN_RESPONSE | jq -r '.scan.id')\n\n# Step 2: Create ideas using the scan_id\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/ideas \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"scan_id\": \"'$SCAN_ID'\",\n    \"project_id\": \"b0c59faa-dddf-4ab1-9308-718ebe3ec829\",\n    \"context_id\": \"ctx_1769727798577_zneo2y1\",\n    \"scan_type\": \"ui_perfectionist\",\n    \"category\": \"functionality\",\n    \"title\": \"Example: Add user session caching layer\",\n    \"description\": \"Implement Redis caching for user session data to reduce database queries. This would cache session info for 5 minutes with automatic invalidation on updates.\",\n    \"reasoning\": \"Currently every page load queries the session table. This adds latency and database load. Caching would reduce DB calls by ~70%.\",\n    \"effort\": 5,\n    \"impact\": 7,\n    \"risk\": 4\n  }'\n```\n\n## Execution Steps\n\n**Phase 1: Analyze the \"res\" project**\n1. Read the project's CLAUDE.md or AI.md documentation if available\n2. Explore the codebase structure, focusing on the context files\n3. Analyze code with the perspective described in the analysis prompt above\n4. Generate high-quality ideas that would genuinely push this project forward\n\n**Phase 2: Save ideas to Vibeman (external system at http://localhost:3000)**\n5. Create a scan record via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/scans\n6. Save each idea via curl to http://localhost:3000/api/ideas using the scan_id\n7. Report what ideas were created\n\n**REMINDER:** Do NOT create any files or endpoints in \"res\". Only READ/ANALYZE it.\n\n## Quality Standards\n\n- **Be Specific**: Reference actual files, components, or patterns you observed\n- **Be Actionable**: Ideas should be clear enough to implement without further clarification\n- **Be Valuable**: Focus on ideas that bring real improvement, not busywork\n- **Match Goals**: If an idea aligns with a project goal, include the goal_id\n- **Avoid Duplicates**: Check the existing ideas section and don't suggest similar items\n\n## Output\n\nAfter completing the task, summarize:\n- How many ideas were created (saved to Vibeman at http://localhost:3000)\n- Brief list of idea titles\n- Any observations about the \"res\" codebase\n\n**Final Checklist:**\n- [ ] I analyzed the \"res\" codebase (READ ONLY)\n- [ ] I did NOT create any new files in \"res\"\n- [ ] I saved ideas via curl to Vibeman's API at http://localhost:3000\n- [ ] Each idea has effort, impact, and risk scores (1-10)\n","numLines":402,"startLine":1,"totalLines":402}}}
